            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When blood glucose concentration decreases, glucagon is released by the pancreas into the blood and is transported to the cells.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 12
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Fig. 6.1 outlines the effect of glucagon on liver cells.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 12
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "figure",
                "id": "fig6.1",
                "caption": "Fig. 6.1",
                "src": "figures/q6_fig6_1.png",
                "alt": "Glucagon signalling at a liver cell membrane, with four structures labelled P, Q, R and S, ATP, an enzyme cascade and a cellular response.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 12
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Identify <b>P</b>,<b> Q</b>,<b> R </b>and<b> S</b> shown in Fig. 6.1.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 12
                }
              },
              {
