            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "The hormone binds outside the cell, while the G-protein relays the signal on the cytoplasmic side. Adenylyl cyclase converts ATP into the second messenger cAMP. The positions of the labels distinguish the receptor, enzyme, G-protein and second messenger.",
                  "refs": [
                    "syllabus:14.1(9)",
                    "ms:a.i#1",
