            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "Glycogenolysis makes stored carbohydrate available as glucose. Glycogenesis stores glucose, while glycolysis and fatty acid synthesis use glucose-derived substrates. The response to low blood glucose favours glucose availability rather than its storage or consumption.",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:a.ii#1",
