      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "type": "extended",
        "marks": 7,
        "source": {
          "qp": 14,
          "ms": 13
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Type 2 diabetes is a condition affecting the homeostatic control of blood glucose concentration. In type 2 diabetes, target cells have a much lower response to insulin and some glucose is excreted in the urine.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Test strips can be used to measure the concentration of glucose in a sample of urine, but many people with type 2 diabetes measure blood glucose concentration using a biosensor.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Explain the principles of operation of a test strip for glucose <b>and</b> suggest advantages for a person with type 2 diabetes of using a biosensor instead of a test strip.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "14.1(11)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 7,
          "instruction": "<i>any <b>four</b> from:</i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "strip contains glucose oxidase and peroxidase <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "strip dipped into urine <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "glucose (and oxygen) reacts with glucose oxidase to produce hydrogen peroxide <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "hydrogen peroxide reacts with peroxidase to produce a colour change <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "text": "colour is matched with a colour chart to give, reading / estimate, of glucose concentration <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 6,
              "text": "<i>any <b>three</b> from:</i><br>quick(er) <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 7,
              "text": "(more) sensitive / accurate / precise <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 8,
              "text": "gives immediate reading <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 9,
              "text": "results can be stored electronically / can be connected to smart phone / AW <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 10,
              "text": "numerical / digital / quantitative / objective <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 11,
              "text": "reusable <b>;</b>"
            }
          ],
          "source": {
            "ms": 13
          }
        },
        "er": [
          "er.q6.b"
        ],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "The urine strip detects glucose already excreted into urine, whereas a blood biosensor measures glucose in a blood sample. A biosensor converts the enzyme reaction into an electrical signal that can be displayed as a numerical concentration.",
